You need to rewrite 2 test files in `/home/eren/Documents/Projects/EaglePoint_Mindflow/TASK-119/repo/unit_tests/` to fix critical gaps where tests mock behavior instead of testing the actual production code.

CONTEXT:
- Tests use `node:test` built-in with `describe/it/beforeEach/afterEach`
- Assertions: `import assert from 'node:assert/strict'`
- DOM mock: `import { setupDOM, teardownDOM } from './dom-mock.js'` - provides `document`, `window`, etc.
- The DOM mock's `document.getElementById` searches both appended children AND innerHTML of children
- `setupDOM()` returns the mock document, sets `globalThis.document`
- `teardownDOM()` cleans up

---

### FILE 1: REWRITE `/home/eren/Documents/Projects/EaglePoint_Mindflow/TASK-119/repo/unit_tests/session-warning.test.js`

The current file (135 lines) simulates the Store subscription pattern instead of importing the actual production component. The production file is at `../frontend/js/components/session-warning.js`:

```javascript
import Store from '../store.js';
import { refreshSession, logout } from '../services/auth-service.js';

let warningEl = null;

export function initSessionWarning() {
  Store.subscribe((key, value) => {
    if (key === 'sessionWarning' && value === true) {
      showSessionWarning();
    }
    if (key === 'sessionExpired' && value === true) {
      hideSessionWarning();
      showExpiredNotice();
    }
  });
}

function showSessionWarning() {
  if (warningEl) return; // duplicate guard
  warningEl = document.createElement('div');
  warningEl.className = 'session-warning-overlay';
  warningEl.innerHTML = `
    <div class="session-warning">
      <h2>Session Expiring</h2>
      <p>Your session will expire in 5 minutes due to inactivity.</p>
      <div class="form-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" id="extend-session-btn">Extend Session</button>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary" id="logout-session-btn">Logout</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  `;
  document.body.appendChild(warningEl);
  document.getElementById('extend-session-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    refreshSession();
    Store.set('sessionWarning', false);
    hideSessionWarning();
  });
  document.getElementById('logout-session-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    logout();
    hideSessionWarning();
    window.location.hash = '/login';
  });
}

function hideSessionWarning() {
  if (warningEl) { warningEl.remove(); warningEl = null; }
}

function showExpiredNotice() {
  const el = document.createElement('div');
  el.className = 'session-warning-overlay';
  el.innerHTML = `
    <div class="session-warning">
      <h2>Session Expired</h2>
      <p>Your session has expired due to inactivity. Please log in again.</p>
      <div class="form-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" id="relogin-btn">Log In</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  `;
  document.body.appendChild(el);
  document.getElementById('relogin-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    el.remove();
    window.location.hash = '/login';
  });
}
```

PROBLEM: session-warning.js imports `refreshSession` and `logout` from `auth-service.js`. auth-service imports `database.js` which needs IndexedDB. We need the IndexedDB mock installed.

The solution: Install IndexedDB/localStorage fakes AND the DOM mock. Then we can import the actual `initSessionWarning` from the production module.

IMPORTANT: `initSessionWarning()` subscribes to the Store. After calling it, you trigger events by calling `Store.set('sessionWarning', true)`. The component then creates DOM elements. The DOM mock supports createElement, appendChild, remove, getElementById (searches innerHTML for `id="..."` patterns), classList, etc.

Write the COMPLETE rewrite with these tests:
1. `initSessionWarning` subscribes to Store (setting sessionWarning triggers warning overlay)
2. Warning overlay has correct structure (session-warning-overlay class, Session Expiring heading)
3. Warning overlay has Extend Session and Logout buttons
4. Duplicate warnings are prevented (set sessionWarning true twice, only one overlay)
5. Setting sessionExpired removes warning and shows expired notice
6. Expired notice has "Session Expired" heading and "Log In" button
